  "english": "22. Sunday, Tone 8 [DK]. Eve of Great Lent (Great Barekendan). See the First Volume up to Transfiguration [Vardavar] for the order of this place.\n\nApril\n\n7. Tuesday, Tone 4 [BK]. Great [Tuesday]. And the Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\n12. Sunday, Tone 1 [ADZ]. Easter: the Day of the Resurrection of Christ. See also the rest according to the order in the First Volume, page 83.\n\nMay\n\n21. Thursday, Tone 8 [DK]. Ascension of Christ.\n31. Sunday, Tone 2 [AK]. Pentecost (Coming of the Holy Spirit). Page 29.\nBarendeand [Eve] of the Fast of Elijah.\n\nJune\n\n7. Sunday, Tone 1 [ADZ]. First Sunday. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Canticle (Harts) [Tone 1, adz]: \"Who came for the salvation of the universe\" (Որ եկիր ի փրկութիւն տիեզերաց). Page 23.\n\nJuly\n\n19. Sunday, Tone 3 [BDZ]. Transfiguration (Vardavar). The dispensation of eating [non-fasting period] is three weeks. Until the Eve of the Fast of the Assumption of the Mother of God, see only the First Volume; look here for the order of the Resurrection Canticles (Harts).\n26. Sunday, Tone 2 [AK]. Second Sunday. Canticle (Harts) [Tone 2, ak]: \"Who came down from heaven\" (Որ ի յերկնից իջեր). Tone 2 [ak] Hymn of the Ascent (Hambartsi): \"You were sent from the Father\" (Առաքեցար ի հօրէ). Page 8.\n\nAugust\n\n2. Sunday, Tone 1 [ADZ]. Third Sunday. Canticle (Harts) [Tone 4, bk]: \"Heavenly host\" (Որ յերկնային զինուոր). Page 25. Tone 1 [adz] Hymn of the Ascent (Hambartsi): \"By thy glorious resurrection, O Lord\" (Փառք յարութեան քո տէր). Page 27.\n9. Sunday, Tone 8 [DK]. Fourth Sunday. Canticle (Harts) [Tone 5, gz]: \"We glorify you\" (Փառաւորեմք զքեզ). Tone 8 [dk] Hymn of the Ascent (Hambartsi): \"When they came\" (Յորժամ եկին) and \"The angel descended\" (Էջ հրեշտակն). Page 28. Eve of the Fast of the Holy Mother of God.\n10. Monday, Tone 1 [ADZ]. Fast of the Holy Mother of God. Canticle (Harts) [Tone 3, bz]: \"Blessed are you, Lord God of our fathers\" (Օրհնեալ տէր աստուած հարցըն).\n16. Sunday, Tone 7 [DDZ]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of God. The dispensation of eating [non-fasting period] is three weeks. See this interval in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place. Page 1.\n\nSeptember\n\nSunday, Tone 4 [BK]. Fourth Sunday. Canticle (Harts) [Tone 6, gk]: \"Ineffable\" (Անճառելի). Tone 4 [bk] Hymn of the Ascent (Hambartsi): \"Christ is risen\" (Քրիստոս յարեաւ). Eve of the Fast of the Holy Cross.\nMonday, Tone 5 [GDZ]. Fast of the Holy Cross. Canticle (Harts) [Tone 4, bk]: \"The captive youths\" (Մանկունքն գերեալք).\nTuesday, Tone 6 [GK]. Fast. Feast of the Nativity of the Holy Virgin from Anna.\nSunday, Tone 7 [DDZ]. Exaltation of the Holy Cross. See up to the tenth Sunday in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\nSunday, Tone 2 [AK]. Second Sunday. Hymn of the Ascent (Hambartsi) [Tone 2, ak]: \"Risen\" (Յարուցեալ). Eve of the Cross of Varag.\nMonday, Tone 3 [BDZ]. Fast of the Cross of Varag. Saint Mamas, and others. Canticle (Harts) [Tone 6, gk]: \"To you, O God\" (Առ քեզ աստուած).\nWednesday, Tone 5 [GDZ]. Fast. Canticle (Harts) [Tone 5, gz]: \"Glorified is your name forever\" (Փառաւորեալ անուն քո յաւիտեան).\nSunday, Tone 1 [ADZ]. Third Sunday. Feast of the Holy Cross of Varag. The dispensation of eating [non-fasting period] is seven weeks.\n\nOctober\n\nSunday, Tone 8 [DK]. Fourth Sunday. Hymn of the Ascent (Hambartsi) [Tone 8, dk]: \"The hosts of angels\" (Հրեշտակացն դասք).\nSunday, Tone 7 [DDZ]. Fifth Sunday. Hymn of the Ascent (Hambartsi) [Tone 7, dz]: \"The women\" (Կանանցն) and \"Awesome\" (Ահագին).\nSunday, Tone 6 [GK]. Sixth Sunday. Hymn of the Ascent (Hambartsi) [Tone 6, gk]: \"The divine\" (Զաստուածային) and \"Thy resurrection\" (Ըզքո յարու թիւնդ).\nSunday, Tone 5 [GDZ]. Seventh Sunday. Discovery of the Holy Cross.\nTuesday, Tone 7 [DDZ]. Saints Hyperichius [and companions], and Severian, etc. Canticle (Harts) [Tone 7, dz]: \"Holy art thou, Lord of hosts\" (Սուրբ ես տէր զօրութեանց).\nWednesday, Tone 8 [DK]. Canticle (Harts) [Tone 5, gz]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord\" (Օրհնեալ ես տէր). For the Covenant.\nSaturday, Tone 3 [BDZ]. All Saints, ancient and new, known and unknown. See also the rest in the First Volume until the end, keeping the order of this place.\n\nNovember\n\nSunday, Tone 4 [BK]. Eighth Sunday. Hymn of the Ascent (Hambartsi) [Tone 4, bk]: \"In the morning\" (Առաւօտեան).",
